<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; Reading path</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: The Indian Ocean World</h1><p class="ws-lede">Monsoon winds, ivory, gold and pepper: the sea that joined East Africa, Arabia, India and the Indies.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/paths/indian-ocean-world">Open the path &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the stops in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the stops from 1 (earliest) to 5 (latest), by when each began: a state&#8217;s founding, a person&#8217;s birth, the date of an event.</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Aksumite Empire</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Kilwa Sultanate</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Chola invasion of Srivijaya</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Srivijaya Empire</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Ming treasure voyages</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Key terms</h2><p class="ws-how">The path uses these words. Explain each one in your own words.</p><ul class="ws-terms"><li><b>Entrepôt</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><b>Ivory trade</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><b>Monsoon</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><b>Porcelain</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><b>Spice trade</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p>Stop 1, <b>Monsoon</b>. The path begins here because: &#8220;The seasonal reversal of winds that governed farming and seaborne trade across the region: sailors timed their voyages to it.&#8221; What does this stop tell you about how the story began?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Stop 5, <b>Chola invasion of Srivijaya</b>: &#8220;In 1025 a Chola fleet from southern India sacked Srivijaya's ports and seized its ruler, breaking the monopoly it lived on.&#8221; Find one detail on its page that supports this, and one question it leaves open.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Stop 9, <b>Malacca</b>: &#8220;Under its sultanate, founded around 1400, it became South-East Asia's leading entrepôt, until the Portuguese captured it in 1511.&#8221; How does this last stop connect to an earlier one?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>The path sums itself up as: &#8220;Monsoon winds, ivory, gold and pepper: the sea that joined East Africa, Arabia, India and the Indies.&#8221; Which stop shows this best? Explain your choice.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/paths/indian-ocean-world. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: The Indian Ocean World</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the stops in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Aksumite Empire <span>from 100 CE</span></li><li>Srivijaya Empire <span>from 650 CE</span></li><li>Kilwa Sultanate <span>from 957 CE</span></li><li>Chola invasion of Srivijaya <span>1025; 1068</span></li><li>Ming treasure voyages <span>1405–1433</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Key terms</h2><dl class="ws-key-terms"><dt>Entrepôt</dt><dd>An entrepôt is a port or trading centre where goods are imported, stored and re-exported, often without further processing.</dd><dt>Ivory trade</dt><dd>The ivory trade is the commerce in elephant tusks, prized for carving and luxury goods.</dd><dt>Monsoon</dt><dd>The monsoon is a seasonal reversal of winds that brings heavy summer rains to South and South-East Asia.</dd><dt>Porcelain</dt><dd>Porcelain is a fine, hard, translucent ceramic first developed in China.</dd><dt>Spice trade</dt><dd>The spice trade was the long-distance commerce in spices such as pepper, cinnamon, cloves and nutmeg from South and Southeast Asia.</dd></dl></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers use details from the pages of the path.</p></section></div></details>
